DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("sin((x^2-5*x+4))");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln((e^(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("[2, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-5, -4, -2, 8, 9})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-5, -4, -2, 8, 9})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-5, -4, -2, 8, 9} U [7, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(-infinity, 12] U {-10, -6, -4, 2, 6, 10}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(({-10, -6, -4, 2, 6, 10} U {-10, -6, -4, 2, 6, 10}) - ({-10, -6, -4, 2, 6, 10}))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-10, -6, -4, 2, 6, 10} U {-10, -6, -4, 2, 6, 10}) U {-10, -6, -4, 2, 6, 10} U (10, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-10, -6, -4, 2, 6, 10} U (10, infinity))) U ((10, infinity))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`0.75+5.57+9.27*11.27`]? [_____]{answer=>110.7929,width=>6}
---

[`9+14*14`] is equal to [_____]{Real(205.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -6, -4, 2, 6, 10\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \leq 12\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(B \cup B) - (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`(B \cup B) \cup B \cup A \cap (B \cup A) \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 7\}`]
- [`B = \{-5, -4, -2, 8, 9\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \geq 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cap (B) \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, -3, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, 1, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -7, -7, -3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-2, 1, 1>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-7, -7, -3>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, -3, -9>") x Compute("<-7, -7, -3>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, -7, -3>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 1, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 7, -2, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, 6, -7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 9, 6, 8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<9, 6, 8>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<8, 6, -7>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, -2, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<7, -2, 10>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<8, 6, -7>") . Compute("<7, -2, 10>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<9, 6, 8>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>4)}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
